    <bpmn:process id="W_W4992" name="W4992. Network Governance, Code-of-Conduct &amp; Installer Relationship Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Program launch; annual governance; installer-relationship review
Frequency: Annual + continuous relationship management
Volume: Quarterly governance across the ~300–500-installer network
Owner: Pro-Referral Network Manager / Legal (VS-100) / Trade Program (VS-43)
Participants: Legal (VS-100), Trade Program (VS-43), Ethics (VS-119), Compliance (VS-22), Installer Council
Source: workflow W4992 — Network Governance, Code-of-Conduct &amp; Installer Relationship Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4992_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4992_Lane1" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4992_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4992_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4992_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4992_Lane2" name="Network Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4992_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4992_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4992_Start4" name="Program launch; annual governance; installer-relationship review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4992_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4992_Task5" name="Establish governance &amp; code-of-conduct: the installer code-of-conduct…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Establish governance &amp; code-of-conduct: the installer code-of-conduct (workmanship, honesty, customer treatment, no-kickback, no-predatory pricing, RA 10667 competition links VS-129), the ethics/ABC expectations (links VS-119/VS-86), the dispute-resolution framework (W5005), and the governance body
Responsible (R): Legal / Network Manager / Ethics / Compliance
Accountable (A): COO / Legal
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4992_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4992_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4992_Task6" name="Manage installer relationships: regular communication, an installer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Manage installer relationships: regular communication, an installer council/forum for feedback, training/enablement (links VS-123/VS-124), recognition/top-performer programs, and retention of preferred installers
Responsible (R): Network Manager / Trade Program / Training
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4992_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4992_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4992_Task7" name="Enforce &amp; remediate: monitor conduct, enforce the code…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enforce &amp; remediate: monitor conduct, enforce the code (warnings/suspension/removal W5005), manage disputes/ethics breaches (VS-119), and ensure fair/non-discriminatory treatment of installers
Responsible (R): Legal / Ethics / Network Manager
Accountable (A): COO / Legal
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4992_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4992_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4992_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4992_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-98 (ensure installer-network vetting &amp; referral integrity.) | - CTL-746: code-of-conduct enforced; disputes/ethics managed; installers treated fairly; retention tracked
Owner: Pro-Referral Network Manager / Legal (VS-100) / Trade Program (VS-43)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
